      "problem": "Consider a $6\\times 7$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =7-5 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
